LSCAN1
# LakeShark conventional scan list - Cape Cod Bay and the Outer Cape
#
# Copy to the SD card and load it:
#
#     python tools/sd_put.py tools/scanlist_cape_cod.lscan scanlist_cape_cod.lscan PORT
#     ch load /sdcard/scanlist_cape_cod.lscan
#
# 'ch load' REPLACES the whole channel list and stops the scanner. This file
# is therefore the complete list, not an addition to one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ROUTE THIS IS BUILT FOR
#
# Yarmouth north and east along the bay to Provincetown, zoned so LOCATION
# filtering walks the list up the Cape on its own:
#
#     0  Countywide, mutual aid and the shared police channels
#     1  Mid Cape        Yarmouth, Dennis
#     2  Lower Cape      Brewster, Harwich, Chatham, Orleans
#     3  Outer Cape      Eastham, Wellfleet, Truro, Provincetown
#     4  Cape Cod Bay    marine, Coast Guard, the canal
#     5  Medical and weather
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT YOU WILL AND WILL NOT HEAR, AND WHY
#
# Town POLICE from Brewster east to Provincetown are talkgroups on the county
# 800 MHz trunk. A conventional scanner cannot follow a trunk, so those towns
# have no police entry here and their absence is the system, not the file.
# Yarmouth PD is conventional 800 and is included. So are the four shared
# Barnstable County VHF police channels, which is where inter-town and
# Provincetown VHF traffic appears.
#
# Town FIRE is the opposite and it is the reason this list is worth carrying:
# every town's fire alarm dispatch is simulcast on its own LOW BAND 33 MHz
# channel, in clear analogue, all the way out to Provincetown.
#
# LOW BAND CAVEAT: 33 MHz sits at the very bottom of the R820T2's range. It
# tunes there, but well below where the tuner is happy. Expect these to be
# the weakest channels in the list and to reward a longer antenna.
#
# Cape Cod National Seashore is P25 and covers the outer beaches.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIELD ORDER
#     name|freq_hz|MODE|zone|latitude|longitude|radius_km|priority
#
# MODE is P25 or NFM only. Every field must be present; '#' starts a comment.
#
# SOURCING: published listener references for the region, cross-checked
# between two of them where possible. None of these has been decoded by the
# board yet, so treat a silent channel as unconfirmed rather than broken.
# One known conflict between sources: Harwich fire alarm is listed as 33.94
# by one and 33.96 by the other. 33.94 is used here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

